invariant: INV-16
file: hash_hw.h
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: hash_hw.h no longer renames sha384_final, so the copies
  hkdf_hw.c and keysched_hw.c hold start each SHA-384 hash on
  sha512_hw.c's calls and end it on sha512.c. Every digest is the same,
  because the two paths keep one state, so no vector fails; a session that
  stated the instructions, or on x86-64 AVX2, runs part of its SHA-384
  calls on the plain C. The script reads the symbols each copy calls, for
  both targets under the pinned clang, and requires the three SHA-384
  calls on their _hw names and none on sha512.c's.

--- old
#define sha384_final sha384_final_hw
--- new
